      "author": "Hollowmere team",
      "story": "Deputy Ray Hale held the Pell substation alone after the county stopped answering. He signed out Lydia Pell's antifungals, locked the station's guns and a Bloom sample from the mine in the evidence room, and took in anyone who came to the fence; the Merrow kids slept in his bunk room for a week. On the night of the first Hum he burned the generator fuel in barrels on the north lot to draw the Hollowed away from the town. It worked too well. They came over the fence when the barrels burned down, and the sick he had locked in the holding cells woke up with them. The kids' sleeping bags are gone. Hale's last log is on the side-office desk with the evidence key on top of it, where he left them before he walked into cell 3 and pulled the door shut behind him.",
